window.LINES={"hello": "Hello, scientist! Welcome to Body Town, where every organ is a building. I'm your guide!", "creak": "Wait. What's that creaking? Something is waking up!", "mumbles_in": "It's a mummy, from Ancient Egypt! His name is Mumbles. He wants to join our tour.", "miccheck": "First, let's check I can hear you. Say: Hello, Mumbles!", "heardyou": "I heard you! Mumbles heard you too. Oops, his bandage fell off!", "nohear": "I can't hear you right now. That's okay. You can tap instead.", "tapmode": "Today you can tap your answers.", "egypt_q": "When Mumbles became a mummy, they threw one organ away. Which one?", "egypt_wrong": "Not that one. They kept that one. Try again!", "egypt_ans": "The brain! They kept the heart inside the body. But they threw the brain away!", "egypt_why": "They thought the heart did the thinking.", "mumbles_heart": "So Mumbles has been thinking with his heart. For thousands of years!", "brain_fact": "Today, we know the brain controls the body. It's the town hall.", "touch": "Touch your head. That's where your brain is. Now touch your heart.", "heart_job": "Your heart pumps blood. It doesn't do the thinking. Sorry, Mumbles!", "question": "The heart and the brain are both organs. So, what do organs do?", "watch": "Remember this bit from the video? Let's watch.", "organ_def": "An organ is a large part of a plant or animal. It does an important job.", "tissues": "Organs are made of different tissues, working together. We'll meet tissues next time.", "func_means": "Every organ has its own function. Function means job.", "buildintro": "Tour guides need the right words. Let's build four of them.", "tapbeats": "Tap the beats in the right order.", "w_organ": "This word means a large part of a plant or animal, with an important job. Two beats.", "w_function": "This word means job. Every organ has one. Two beats.", "w_diaphragm": "This one is a sheet of muscle under your lungs. It helps you breathe. Three beats.", "w_intestine": "This one is a long tube. Food goes into it after your stomach. Three beats.", "notyet": "Not that one yet. Which beat comes next?", "built": "You built it!", "drum": "Now tap the drum once for each beat, and say the beats with me.", "sayword": "Now say the whole word.", "again": "Let's try once more, slowly. Listen.", "yousay": "Now you say it.", "goodtry": "Good try! We'll practise that one again another day.", "n_organ": "Organ.", "n_function": "Function.", "n_diaphragm": "Diaphragm.", "n_intestine": "Intestine.", "s_or": "Or.", "s_gan": "Gan.", "s_func": "Funk.", "s_tion": "Tion.", "s_di": "Dye.", "s_a": "Uh.", "s_phragm": "Fram.", "s_in": "In.", "s_tes": "Tess.", "s_tine": "Tin.", "wordsdone": "Four words built! Now let's explore Body Town.", "map_intro": "Here's the map of Body Town. We'll start upstairs. I say a building, you find it.", "map_wrong": "Not that one. Look again. Is it higher, or lower?", "f_brain": "Find the brain.", "j_brain": "The brain controls the body. It's the town hall.", "f_skin": "Find the skin. Careful, it's everywhere!", "j_skin": "Skin is an organ too. It's the biggest organ in your body!", "j_skin2": "Skin protects you. It also lets you sense things, like heat and touch.", "f_windpipe": "Find the windpipe.", "j_windpipe": "The windpipe takes air to and from your lungs. Scientists call it the trachea.", "f_lungs": "Find the lungs. You have two.", "j_lungs": "Lungs get oxygen into your blood, for respiration. They excrete carbon dioxide too.", "f_heart": "Find the heart.", "j_heart": "The heart pumps blood. It's the town's pumping station.", "heart_where": "See? It sits between your lungs, a little to your left.", "f_diaphragm": "Find the diaphragm.", "j_diaphragm": "The diaphragm is a muscular sheet under your lungs. It helps you breathe.", "map_done": "Upstairs is done! Now let's go downstairs.", "lunch_intro": "Downstairs, we follow your lunch through Body Town. Let's watch.", "gssl": "Our trick for the food path is Good Snacks Stay Long.", "gssl_order": "Put the four organs in order, from your mouth down.", "gssl_wrong": "Not that one yet. Say Good Snacks Stay Long, slowly.", "g_gullet": "Gullet. It takes food from your mouth to your stomach. Its science name is oesophagus.", "g_stomach": "Stomach. It breaks up food.", "g_small": "Small intestine. It breaks up food more, then absorbs it into your blood.", "g_large": "Large intestine. It takes water out of the food your body doesn't need.", "nutrition": "Getting food into your blood gives you nutrition. That's the N in Mrs Gren!", "f_liver": "Now find the liver. It's big, and next to your stomach.", "j_liver": "The liver makes, destroys and stores some substances. It's the town's factory and warehouse.", "f_kidneys": "Find the kidneys. There are two, at the back.", "j_kidneys": "The kidneys clean your blood. They make urine, to excrete waste.", "kidney_touch": "Put your hands on your back, just above your waist. Your kidneys are in there!", "f_bladder": "Find the bladder.", "j_bladder": "The bladder stores urine, until you go to the toilet.", "match_intro": "Quick quiz! Give each organ its job card.", "match_wrong": "Not quite. Think about that building's job.", "snack_done": "Every building visited! Body Town is very busy.", "breaktime": "You've worked hard. Time for a brain break, with Mumbles!", "bb_intro": "Stand up! Let's do the Mummy Moves. Arms out straight, like Mumbles!", "bb_walk": "Walk like a mummy. Stiff legs. Slow steps. Mmmmm!", "bb_neck": "Stop! Touch your neck. That's your windpipe.", "bb_chest": "Hands on your chest. Breathe in slowly. Your lungs fill up.", "bb_ribs": "Now hands just under your ribs. Your diaphragm. Breathe out slowly.", "bb_kid": "Hands on your back, above your waist. Hello, kidneys!", "bb_trick": "Quick! Touch the organ that does your thinking!", "bb_caught": "Your head? Yes! Ha, Mumbles touched his heart again. Oh, Mumbles!", "bb_done": "Great moving! Sit down. Now let's meet Mrs Gren's organ teams.", "teams_intro": "Remember Mrs Gren? Organs work in teams for her life processes. Tap every organ in the team.", "team_wrong": "Not in this team. Think about its job.", "t_oxygen": "Respiration first. Which organ gets oxygen into your blood?", "t_oxygen_a": "The lungs! Oxygen goes into your blood, for respiration.", "t_food": "Nutrition team! Which three organs get food into your body?", "t_food_a": "Gullet, stomach and small intestine! The large intestine only takes out water.", "t_waste": "Excretion team! Which three organs help get rid of waste?", "t_waste_a": "Kidneys, lungs and liver! Kidneys make urine. Lungs excrete carbon dioxide. The liver destroys harmful substances.", "t_store": "Which two organs store waste, until you go to the toilet?", "t_store_a": "The bladder stores urine. The rectum stores poo. Mumbles can't stop giggling!", "t_sense": "Sensitivity team! Which organs help you sense things around you?", "t_sense_a": "Skin, eyes, ears, nose and tongue! Your eyes detect light, so you can see.", "whale_intro": "Big news! Scientists found a new organ, in a whale's chin!", "whale_job": "It senses tiny animals called krill. Then the whale opens wide. Gulp!", "whale_q": "Sensing krill. Which life process is that?", "whale_a": "Sensitivity! The new organ senses things, like your skin and eyes.", "whale_brain": "Which organ gets the message, and tells the whale's jaw to move?", "whale_brain_a": "The brain! It controls the body. Even a whale's body.", "teams_done": "Every team is complete! Mrs Gren would be proud.", "park_intro": "Welcome to Body Town Park! Do plants have organs too? Yes, they do!", "rslf": "Plants have four main organs. Our trick, bottom to top: Real Snails Love Flowers.", "plant_tap": "Help the snail climb. Tap each organ, from the bottom to the top.", "plant_wrong": "Start at the bottom. Real Snails Love Flowers.", "p_roots": "Roots hold the plant in place. They take in water, and small amounts of other substances.", "p_stem": "The stem carries substances around the plant. It holds up the leaves and flowers.", "p_leaves": "Leaves trap sunlight, to make food for the plant.", "p_flowers": "Flowers are for reproduction. They make seeds.", "leaf_q": "So, which plant organ makes food?", "w_photosynthesis": "This word means making food, using light. Five beats. Take your time.", "n_photosynthesis": "Photosynthesis.", "s_pho": "Foe.", "s_to": "Toe.", "s_syn": "Sin.", "s_the": "Thuh.", "s_sis": "Sis.", "recipe": "Photosynthesis needs three things. Pick them for the leaf.", "r_light": "Light! Photosynthesis only happens when there is light.", "r_co2": "Carbon dioxide, from the air.", "r_water": "Water, taken in by the roots.", "park_wrong": "Hmm, think again. What does a leaf really need?", "expt_intro": "Let's test it! One plant sits on a sunny windowsill. One goes into Mumbles' dark tomb.", "expt_q": "A week later. Which plant made more food?", "expt_a": "The sunny one! With less light, less food is made.", "report": "Scientists write reports with the same headings. Then everyone can understand and compare them.", "report_order": "Put the headings in order. Our trick: A Pet Mummy Really Can't Eat.", "report_wrong": "Not that one yet. Say the trick slowly.", "h_aim": "Aim. What we want to find out.", "h_pred": "Prediction. What we think will happen.", "h_method": "Method. What we did.", "h_results": "Results. What we found.", "h_concl": "Conclusion. More photosynthesis happens when there is more light!", "h_eval": "Evaluation. How we could do it better next time.", "lily": "Shady plants grow big leaves, to catch light. Giant water lily leaves are three metres across!", "store_q": "Plants store some food in storage organs. Which two of these are storage organs?", "store_a": "A carrot and a potato! They're full of the plant's stored food.", "park_done": "The park is done! Now, to Body Town Hospital.", "hosp_intro": "Welcome to Body Town Hospital! How do doctors find out what's wrong inside you?", "stem": "They use STEM. Science, technology, engineering and maths. All four are linked.", "xray": "In eighteen ninety-five, scientists found X-rays. X-rays show the bones inside you.", "xray_q": "This patient may have a broken leg. What should the doctor use?", "xray_a": "An X-ray! It shows the bones inside the leg.", "scan": "X-rays led on to body scanners. Doctors can see a heart pumping, without cutting!", "heart_check": "A stethoscope lets doctors hear your heartbeat and breathing. They can measure your pulse too.", "method_intro": "Doctors solve problems like scientists. Put the steps in order.", "method_wrong": "Not yet. What comes first?", "ps_idea": "Think of an idea, to explain the problem.", "ps_test": "Test the idea.", "ps_evid": "The test results are evidence.", "ps_concl": "Evidence helps you reach a conclusion.", "ps_diag": "A doctor's conclusion is called a diagnosis.", "w_diagnosis": "This word means a doctor's conclusion. Knowing what is wrong. Four beats.", "n_diagnosis": "Diagnosis.", "s_ag": "Ag.", "s_no": "No.", "diag_means": "Dia means through. Gnosis means knowing. Knowing what is wrong!", "case_intro": "Case file one! This patient has yellow skin.", "case_ev": "A urine test finds a yellow substance too. That's more evidence.", "case_q": "Which organ is the problem?", "case_a": "The liver! The diagnosis is liver disease.", "symp_intro": "More patients! Use the symptoms. Which organ has a problem?", "sy1": "This patient makes only a small amount of urine.", "sy2": "This patient finds it hard to breathe.", "sy3": "This patient has a very fast pulse.", "sy4": "This patient has a sore chest after eating.", "hosp_wrong": "Not quite. Check the clues again, doctor.", "chart_q": "This chart shows deaths from organ diseases in the UK. Which bar is tallest?", "chart_a": "Heart disease. It's a major cause of death in the UK.", "jobs_intro": "Lots of jobs need organ know-how. Match each person to their job.", "job_cardio": "A cardiologist is a heart doctor. Cardio means heart.", "job_physio": "A physiotherapist helps people recover from muscle and bone injuries. Even top athletes!", "job_path": "A pathologist studies organs and tissues, to find out what went wrong. Some study mummies!", "train": "Nurses need organ know-how too. Doctors train at university for six or seven years!", "hosp_done": "Every case solved! Brilliant work, doctor.", "teach_intro": "Oh dear. Mumbles told me some \"facts\", and now I'm muddled. Can you teach me?", "m1": "The heart does the thinking. Mumbles' heart told me so. Is that right?", "m1_fix": "Of course! The brain controls the body. The heart pumps blood.", "m2": "Skin isn't an organ. It's just a wrapper, like Mumbles' bandages. Is that right?", "m2_fix": "Oh! Skin is an organ. It's the biggest organ in your body!", "m3": "Plants get their food from the soil. Is that right?", "m3_fix": "I see! Plants make their own food in their leaves, by photosynthesis.", "m4": "The large intestine absorbs your food into your blood. Is that right?", "m4_fix": "Silly me! The small intestine absorbs food. The large intestine takes out water.", "m5": "Your lungs only take air in. Is that right?", "m5_fix": "Oh yes! Lungs get oxygen in. They excrete carbon dioxide too.", "teach_wrong": "Hmm, are you sure? Let's think it through together.", "teach_done": "You're a brilliant teacher! I'm not muddled any more.", "finish": "Tour complete! You've visited every building in Body Town.", "bigideas": "Remember: every organ has a function. Plants have organs too. Leaves make food using light.", "mumbles_bye": "Mumbles says thank you, from the bottom of his heart. Not his brain!", "cert": "Here is your certificate. You are a Body Town Organ Expert!", "next": "Next time, we look inside organs, at tissues. See you soon, scientist!", "p1": "Well done!", "p2": "Brilliant!", "p3": "You got it!", "p4": "Super thinking!", "p5": "Great job!", "p6": "Fantastic!", "p7": "Yes! Even Mumbles is dancing!"};
